# Docker containers commends
## Administrative commends
### List of running containres
```sh
# List of containers
docker ps

# Containers logs
docker logs -f pihole
## -f Follow logs
## pihole - container name this can be either name or ID
```

If you running multiple container with compose.yml use below to see all container logs
- Navigate to *docker-compose.yml* | *compose.yml* location
- The logs started container name followed by the transaction

```sh
cd /opt/application/
docker compose logs -f
```

### Docker Compose
Docker compose if more reliable for live app, application come back online after reboot without manual intervension

#### Run docker compose containers
- Navigate to application directory where the compose-yml exist
```sh
docker compose up -d
# -d - detach mode where running backround